  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_035 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.542, cost=2.94 GPU hrs). Across experiments, avgpool consistently outperforms transformer (and is cheaper), weighted beats concat, and imagenet_vit_l beats resnet50. The only major untested variable in this best-performing pipeline is the RNA encoder (only scgpt has been tested). Question: Does scvi_n200 match or beat scgpt when paired with the best image encoder and aggregation/fusion settings? This directly tests whether the more complex scgpt encoder is necessary or whether a lighter encoder suffices. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a single-variable change from the current best, keeping the proven avgpool+weighted+vit_l pipeline intact, so any accuracy difference is cleanly attributable to the RNA encoder. If scvi_n200 performs comparably, we confirm a cheaper path forward; if it outperforms, we find a new best. Expected relative cost: similar to or slightly below config_035 (~2.5–3.0 GPU hrs), since scvi_n200 is a smaller encoder than scgpt while the image and aggregation components remain the same."
